WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.567
A useful routing trace should be short and factual.

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:08.847
For one run, you might record: route equals policy and order.

00:00:08.847 --> 00:00:11.752
Policy search returned three chunks.

00:00:11.752 --> 00:00:16.062
Order lookup says delivered on September twenty ninth.

00:00:16.062 --> 00:00:21.034
Evidence is sufficient. Next action is generate answer.

00:00:21.664 --> 00:00:24.816
That trace is enough to understand the trajectory.

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:33.906
Good trace fields include the action, validated arguments, source I D's, a score or result summary, latency, errors,

00:00:33.906 --> 00:00:40.956
and the next route. Do not store secrets or unnecessary personal information.

00:00:40.956 --> 00:00:45.276
Do not dump huge raw tool responses into logs.

00:00:45.276 --> 00:00:48.464
And do not depend on hidden private reasoning.

00:00:49.188 --> 00:00:53.545
A concise trace is valuable for grading student projects too.

00:00:53.545 --> 00:00:58.282
It lets you show not just the final answer, but how the system got there.
